    "headroom_beyond_already_observed_movement": 1.18,
    "stated_plainly": "A reconstruction that moved as much again as the worst movement already measured would put the weakest delivered frame within about 18% of the floor.",
    "why_this_is_not_an_argument_for_retuning": "It is derived from measured movement, not from the nine frames the threshold was chosen on, so it argues for validating the edge against frames outside these nine rather than for moving the floor on them."
  },
  "what_this_does_not_establish": "That the floor's edge is correct. It establishes that the mask question could not have moved the gate, and that the statistic choice was the right one for a reason that is now measured rather than asserted.",
